    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">On April 24, 2025, Kansas enacted legislation to change its apportionment methodology from three-factor to single-factor sales, effective for tax years beginning January 1, 2027. Following the enactment, we revalued certain deferred tax balances impacted by the change in future state apportionment methodology and recorded a net regulatory asset to offset deferred taxes associated with rate base. We will begin amortization of the net regulatory asset after the effective date.
          <br/>
          <br/>The net amortization of net (excess)/deficient deferred income taxes is included with the amortization of net (excess)/deficient deferred income taxes associated with state income tax changes.
          <br/>
          <br/>The total net (excess)/deficient deferred income tax amortization of $(376,543) discussed further in the note shown on page 278, is reported as the input to page 3, line 73a in our formula rate tariff.
        </span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
