        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Note A of our formula rate tariff requires that the balances of 190, 281, 282 and 283 are to be adjusted by any amounts in contra accounts identified as regulatory assets or liabilities related to Financial Accounting Standards Board ("FASB") Accounting Standards Codification 740 - Income Taxes ("ASC 740"), and exclude deferred taxes on true-up, regulatory assets, goodwill, facilities, or premium on asset acquisitions unless the underlying amount is included in rate base. Pursuant to this requirement we have included a reconciliation of the amounts reported on the FERC Form No. 1 to the adjusted amounts included in our formula rate tariff when reference is made to page 277, line 9, column k, as shown below.</span>
