    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-28" id="fn-28" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Federal tax adjustments are related to other income tax receivables recorded within account 143.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-29" id="fn-29" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ITC Great Plains operates within the states of Kansas and Oklahoma and utilizes a single aggregate tax rate for tax accounting. The tax rate is calculated using the respective statutory tax rate and apportionment factor formula for each state.&#160;</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-30" id="fn-30" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ITC Great Plains has property tax within the states of Kansas and Oklahoma.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-31" id="fn-31" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ITC Great Plains has filings within the states of Iowa, Kansas, Michigan and Oklahoma.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-32" id="fn-32" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other taxes primarily includes Sales and Use tax and other taxes and also includes certain activity related to 2024.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-33" id="fn-33" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The activity also reflects prior year adjustments to actual and certain tax year 2024 payments.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-34" id="fn-34" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Payroll taxes are paid by ITC Holdings Corp. to the various governmental agencies and allocated to its subsidiaries including ITC Great Plains LLC.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-35" id="fn-35" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Federal income taxes also reflects certain tax year 2024 activity.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-36" id="fn-36" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">State income taxes also reflects certain tax year 2024 activity.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-37" id="fn-37" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Total other tax is used when reference is to page 263, column l within page 3, line 65, column 3 of our formula rate tariff.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-38" id="fn-38" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Total property tax is used when reference is to page 263, column l within page 3, line 63, column 3 of our formula rate tariff.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-39" id="fn-39" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Total payroll tax is used when reference is to page 263, column l within page 3, line 60, column 3 of our formula rate tariff.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-40" id="fn-40" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The amount represents balances previously recorded to account 397 prior to implementation of FERC Order 898.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-41" id="fn-41" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amounts shown as transfers in column (f) from account 391 were solely for the purpose of implementing FERC Order 898 and represent transfers of computer hardware, software and communication equipment to newly established plant accounts 351.1, 351.2, 351.3, 397.1, 397.2, 397.3.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-42" id="fn-42" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The depreciation rates shown in column (e) are straight line rates which when applied to monthly plant balances will uniformly recover the unrecovered cost, adjusted for net salvage, over the remaining life of the plant.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-43" id="fn-43" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Average Remaining Life shown in column (g) is based on the latest approved depreciation study, which is based on balances as of December 31, 2022.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-44" id="fn-44" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Contains plant co-owned with Sunflower Electric Power Corporation, which is not an associated company. See Footnote 9, Jointly Owned Utility Plant/Coordinated Services on page 123.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-45" id="fn-45" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The transformer at Elm Creek is jointly owned with Sunflower Electric Power Corporation, which is not an associated company. See Footnote 9, Jointly Owned Utility Plant/Coordinated Services on page 123.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-46" id="fn-46" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The 'Other Accounts' balance represents charges for certain political and related activities in account 426.4.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-47" id="fn-47" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This includes amounts recorded on a modified Massachusetts Formula allocation policy as described in page 123 Note 4 under "-Cost Assignment" and page 123 Note 10 Related-Party Transactions.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-48" id="fn-48" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This includes amounts recorded on a modified Massachusetts Formula allocation policy as described in page 123 Note 4 under "-Cost Assignment" and page 123 Note 10 Related-Party Transactions.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-49" id="fn-49" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This includes amounts recorded on a modified Massachusetts Formula allocation policy as described in page 123 Note 4 under "-Cost Assignment" and page 123 Note 10 Related-Party Transactions.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-50" id="fn-50" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rental amounts are assigned to ITC Affiliates based on a standardized methodology which identifies, records, and assigns costs related to shared assets and leased facilities to the affiliated business units benefiting from the usage of those shared assets. This standard methodology is generally considered an extension of ITC&#8217;s Direct Assignment Policy.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-51" id="fn-51" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Deferred taxes related to acquisition premium and Co-development intangible plant are included in other income and deductions, which is excluded from the formula rate tariff.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-52" id="fn-52" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other minor plant timing differences associated with below the line operating expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-53" id="fn-53" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">No information is provided in column (h) for billing demand, since these pages report Transmission Revenue dollars by schedule and demand information is not readily available and is not used for billing purposes.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-54" id="fn-54" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">All schedules use SPP as a billing agent.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-55" id="fn-55" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Account 425 is the amortization expense associated with our intangible plant assets relating to payments made under Section 7.1, 7.2, 7.3 and 7.4 of certain Co-Development Agreements. Based on the Settlement Agreement in Docket ER09-548, these amounts are to be identified in the FERC Form No. 1 and are excluded from the formula rate tariff. Account 425 is not included in the formula rate tariff.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-56" id="fn-56" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents borrowings under the revolving credit agreement.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-57" id="fn-57" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents borrowings under the revolving credit agreement.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-58" id="fn-58" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents repayments of the revolving credit agreement.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-59" id="fn-59" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents repayments of the revolving credit agreement of $36,900,000 and redemption of long-term debt of $50,000,000.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-60" id="fn-60" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents cash balance in accounts 131 and 136.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-61" id="fn-61" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents cash balance in accounts 131 and 136.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-62" id="fn-62" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other minor timing differences associated with operating income and expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-63" id="fn-63" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other minor timing differences associated with below the line operating income and expenses.</link:footnote>
